# What NOT to ship in the .vsix.
#
# vsce packages the WORKING TREE, not the git index, so `.gitignore` buys nothing
# here: a file git refuses to track is still shipped to every user unless it is
# named below as well. That is one rule ("this is local-only") written in two
# places, and the second place was missing the local notes — CLAUDE.md, with its
# internal hostnames, went out in every locally built .vsix from v1.5.0 to v1.7.0.
#
# So: every gitignored path is named here too, except `dist/`, which IS the
# product. test/packaging.test.ts holds the two files to that.
#
# Paths vsce already excludes by default (`.vscode-test`, `.DS_Store`, …) are
# still listed explicitly. What ships should be legible from this file alone,
# rather than from which defaults a packaging tool happens to carry.

# Local-only notes and scratch state (gitignored).
CLAUDE.md
.superpowers/**
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store

# Sources, tests and their outputs.
src/**
test/**
test-integration/**
dist-test/**
coverage/**
.vscode-test/**
.vscode-test-web/**
demo-workspace/**

# Tooling and repo furniture.
.vscode/**
.claude/**
.github/**
docs/**
node_modules/**
scripts/**
esbuild.mjs
esbuild.test.mjs
.vscode-test.mjs
vite.config.ts
vitest.config.ts
tsconfig.json
**/*.map
media/screenshots/**
media/icons/**
*.vsix
